---
source: crates/pith-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: text
---
the pith kernel

Usage: pith [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check    Elaborate the module at PATH and report its errors and warnings
  explore  Show types, rules, entries, interfaces, metadata, and implementation tiers
  fmt      Write the canonical spelling of the module at PATH
  run      Evaluate a named entry and render its value
  explain  Evaluate a named entry and explain its last invalidation
  graph    Inspect entry selection, action plans, and recorded dependencies
  exec     Evaluate an entry to pith.Exec and replace this process with it
  store    Inspect and admit content
  state    Inspect engine state
  gc       Report what a collection would reclaim
  diff     Compare the workspace declaration with its lock; requires a workspace
  update   Resolve and write the workspace lock; requires a workspace
  add      Add a dependency to the workspace; requires a workspace
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --output <OUTPUT>  Output shape. Defaults to pretty on a TTY, plain otherwise [possible values: pretty, plain, json]
      --store <DIR>      Content store root. Defaults to $PITH_HOME/store [env: PITH_STORE=]
      --state <FILE>     Engine state root. Defaults to $PITH_HOME/state.db [env: PITH_STATE=]
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

Workspace commands require a workspace; diff, update, and add are visible here but arrive with M-14.
